edit(p, '''5. `--verify` checks 5 of 16 baselines (H13).
6. The hygiene items L1, L3 and L6 are not done.''', '''5. `--verify` checks 5 of 16 baselines (H13).
6. The hygiene items L1, L3 and L6 are not done.

**Status 14 October 2026 (go-live controls, later the same day, uncommitted in the working tree):** the controls and small defects below were built after the table above was written; the table is kept as it was. Tests: `tests/Feature/Eir/GoLiveControlsTest.php` (10 tests) and additions to `TakeonLandingServiceTest`, `MegaFarmProgrammeSeparationTest`, `LoanBookBuildServiceTest`, `GlFeeRouteTest`, `FliRouteServiceTest` and `StagingClassifierTest`.

| Id | Status now | What was built |
|---|---|---|
| C2 | BUILT | The Internal Grading writer reads `remaining_tenor` as months and takes the year that covers it (`App\\Support\\Tenor::yearsCovering`); a loan with no mapping, tenor or PD for its tenor is left unchanged and named, not given a PD of nil |
| C9 | BUILT | The residual is closed: `FliRouteService::approveFit` refuses a null approver or a fit with no named proposer; `fli:apply --approve` needs `--user` and no longer accepts `--bootstrap` |
| H4 | PARTLY | `ReportingPeriodLock::assertOpen` is now called by `MegaFarmEclService::run` and by the legacy writers (transition matrix and its cumulative form, cumulative LGD, collateral allocation and customer LGD, internal grading). The collateral allocation also wrote every month of a contract; it now writes the allocation's own month. Still open: `EirCalculationService` (another work stream) |
| H9 | PARTLY | Schedule approval reads `schedule_approval_control` at the date of approval: under "Second person must approve" the approver must be named and must not be the person who generated the draft (`contract_eir.schedule_prepared_by`); the bootstrap approves under its label, recorded in `schedule_approver_label`. Still open: the EIR lock by administrator override in the bootstrap (see M8) |
| H11 | BUILT | `staging_thresholds` rows are proposed and approved by two people (`StagingThresholdService`, Settings, Staging basis), forward only and never into a locked month; staging reads only approved rows. The legacy `StagingClassifier` reads the rule at the import's period end and stops with the reason when none is in force (no 31/181 fallback) |
| M2 | PARTLY | The fee GL gate is now a landing gate that refuses a pack (`PackGates` `fee_gl`, level ERROR) where a month of `GL_04a` differs from the trial balance; a month with no trial balance yet is listed and checked again by `eir:build-gl-fees`, which the month-end now runs. `MF_03` postings are gated against the master. The ISO-date, balance-history and month-end-row gates still only warn |
| M8 | PARTLY | The take-on Build is proposed and approved (`takeon_build_requests`); the bootstrap approves it and the schedules under its label. The bootstrap still locks each EIR with the administrator override: the label needs a parameter on `EirCalculationService::lock`, which is another work stream's file |
| M9 | BUILT | `12m_pd` is dropped from the PD the sensitivity and the overlay read (`coalesce(pd_prefli, pd_value)`); `lifetime_pd` is decimal(12,8) (migration `2026_10_14_220000_go_live_controls`) |
| M12 | PARTLY | The 17 settings no engine reads are marked "recorded, not yet applied" in the Governance Centre with what the engine does instead (`GovernanceService::notYetApplied`); `schedule_approval_control` is read; the readers that fell back to a constant now stop (the FLI route, the build method, `dpd_basis`, the Mega Farm settings and share, the scenario rules). `governed_parameters` remains |
| M15 | BUILT | Reversals (306, 343, 901) are paired with the posting they reverse (`EirLedgerCashService::pairReversals`; 29 paired and 11 unpaired on the clone `maiic_ifrs9_controls`); a contract drawn above its sanction is flagged (`contract_eir.over_sanction_amount`; 2 on the clone); the `RATE_BASIS` alias is removed and the file importer takes the rate type from `RATE_TYPE`, else the Interest Policy |
| L5 | PARTLY | The contractual rate is a fraction and a value above 1 is refused, not rescaled; `TRANSAMT` commas are stripped in `BaselineService`; `lifetime_pd` widened. The 30/360 and 30E/360 rule in `CalculateEirService` is another work stream's file |''')
